# strapd core package list for Debian 13 (trixie), restricted to what trixie's
# own archive carries. install.sh installs these with `apt-get install`.
#
# This is the Debian translation of arch/install/strapd-base.packages. Package
# names are Debian's, which differ from Arch's more often than not; the notable
# renames, so an auditor can follow them back:
#
#   avahi -> avahi-daemon            docker -> docker.io
#   cups-pdf -> printer-driver-cups-pdf   fd -> fd-find (binary: fdfind)
#   mako -> mako-notifier            bat  -> bat (binary: batcat)
#   networkmanager -> network-manager     nss-mdns -> libnss-mdns
#   sushi -> gnome-sushi             tldr -> tealdeer
#   zbar -> zbar-tools               tesseract -> tesseract-ocr(+-eng)
#   python-gobject -> python3-gi     nautilus-python -> python3-nautilus
#   gvfs-{mtp,nfs,smb} -> gvfs-backends (one package covers all three)
#   fcitx5-gtk -> fcitx5-frontend-gtk3 + -gtk4
#   fcitx5-qt  -> fcitx5-frontend-qt5 + -qt6
#   qemu-user-static-binfmt -> qemu-user-static   greetd-tuigreet -> tuigreet
#   libreoffice-fresh -> libreoffice   qt6-imageformats -> qt6-image-formats-plugins
#
# Folded into another package (so not listed): bluez-utils -> bluez.
#
# NOT here, because trixie does not package them, see strapd-external.packages:
# the modern Wayland stack strapd is built on. niri, mangowc, the Noctalia shell
# (and its quickshell), xwayland-satellite, hyprpicker. uwsm is not packaged
# either, but it is load-bearing (strapd-session execs `uwsm start`), so the
# install builds it from source in install/config/build-uwsm.sh rather than
# leave it to the external list; its runtime deps (python3-xdg, python3-dbus)
# and dbus-user-session are here. With uwsm built, sway installs and runs from
# this list; niri and mango still need building from strapd-external.packages.
#
# Dropped as Arch-only (no Debian meaning): expac, pacman-contrib,
# kernel-modules-hook. Substituted with the nearest Debian equivalent where the
# exact package is absent: fonts-jetbrains-mono for the Nerd-patched font (the
# Nerd variant is not in Debian), tealdeer for the tldr client.

